WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.218 --> 00:00:01.603
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.603 --> 00:00:05.874
Today's message is Create
Memorable Experiences.

00:00:05.874 --> 00:00:08.597
Over to you, Juergen Klopp.

00:00:08.597 --> 00:00:10.792
(electronic explosion)

00:00:10.792 --> 00:00:13.276
(rooster crowing)

00:00:13.276 --> 00:00:15.675
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:19.946
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:21.049
- [Interviewer] How would you describe

00:00:21.049 --> 00:00:22.765
your footballing philosophy?

00:00:22.765 --> 00:00:23.598
- Lively.

00:00:25.421 --> 00:00:29.421
I think it's, it's not
the smartest way, I know,

00:00:31.545 --> 00:00:33.550
- Success is the smartest way.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.380
- Yeah, that's how it is,
successful, it's cool too,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.447
but first of all, having memorable games,

00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:42.270
in a row, that's my first target,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.208
that the people really
want to see the next game,

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:46.285
you leave the stadium, you
want to see the next game,

00:00:46.285 --> 00:00:47.830
you can't wait for the next game.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.418
That's what football should be.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:52.064
And if you can do this very often,

00:00:52.064 --> 00:00:54.357
then you will be successful, 100%.

00:00:54.357 --> 00:00:55.696
- So I think this is a
message that entrepreneurs

00:00:55.696 --> 00:00:56.712
can learn from too.

00:00:56.712 --> 00:00:59.155
I think that we want to
create memorable experiences

00:00:59.155 --> 00:00:59.988
in our business.

00:00:59.988 --> 00:01:02.125
I think you should be
excited about the work

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:03.834
that you're going to do every day.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.620
And yes, you're going to have bad times,

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.017
and not everything is going
to be amazing and rosy,

00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:10.255
but, at the end of the
day, you should be excited

00:01:10.255 --> 00:01:11.191
about the work you're doing.

00:01:11.191 --> 00:01:13.754
You should feel like the
work that you are creating

00:01:13.754 --> 00:01:16.234
is valuable, is important, is memorable,

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:19.442
that what you did today
is going to matter.

00:01:19.442 --> 00:01:21.433
I think that's why a lot of
people become entrepreneurs

00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:22.935
is because you want your work to matter,

00:01:22.935 --> 00:01:25.334
because you don't want
to work for the man,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.818
you don't want to work at some
job where you're not important,

00:01:27.818 --> 00:01:29.322
where you're not havin' an impact.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:33.060
And so I think, if you
are not in that situation

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:33.919
where you feel like the work

00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:36.194
that you are doing is important,

00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:39.118
is meaningful, is valuable to yourself and

00:01:39.118 --> 00:01:40.986
to the community, to
the people around you,

00:01:40.986 --> 00:01:42.937
to you customers, then
that's when you need

00:01:42.937 --> 00:01:44.853
to start to change something.

00:01:44.853 --> 00:01:46.684
I think a lot of entrepreneurs
who go in to business

00:01:46.684 --> 00:01:48.191
just try to make a lot of money,

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:49.453
those are the ones who fail,

00:01:49.453 --> 00:01:51.002
because they're not
tryin' to have an impact,

00:01:51.002 --> 00:01:53.317
because they're not tryin' to
create something memorable,

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:54.496
because they're not
tryin' to create something

00:01:54.496 --> 00:01:56.078
that they can show
their grandkids and say,

00:01:56.078 --> 00:01:57.624
"Look at what I did.

00:01:57.624 --> 00:01:59.089
"Look at what I created.

00:01:59.089 --> 00:02:00.674
"Look at the impact that I had."

00:02:00.674 --> 00:02:03.242
That needs to be part of your motivation,

00:02:03.242 --> 00:02:05.558
that every day you wake up
and you're doing something

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.790
that's going to matter to somebody.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.253
It fuels you.

00:02:09.253 --> 00:02:10.676
And I think if you look
at yourself in the mirror

00:02:10.676 --> 00:02:12.345
for too many days in a row, and you find

00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:14.779
that the work you're doing is meaningless,

00:02:14.779 --> 00:02:16.447
is not really havin' a big impact,

00:02:16.447 --> 00:02:18.762
then you owe it to
yourself to make a change.

00:02:18.762 --> 00:02:20.873
You owe it to yourself,
you owe it to your family,

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:21.727
you owe it to your community, you owe it

00:02:21.727 --> 00:02:23.437
to the world, to make a change.

00:02:23.437 --> 00:02:24.818
To do something different.

00:02:24.818 --> 00:02:28.150
And you apply the same
strategies, same mindset mentality

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.128
to everything that you do.

00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:31.198
You apply it to your
relationships, you apply it

00:02:31.198 --> 00:02:33.960
to your friendships, you
apply it to your life.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.294
You want the time that
you spend on anything

00:02:37.294 --> 00:02:38.473
to matter.

00:02:38.473 --> 00:02:39.976
And one of the things that I routinely do

00:02:39.976 --> 00:02:42.537
is a self-audit, at
least every couple months

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:43.883
I'll do a self-audit, and look at

00:02:43.883 --> 00:02:47.092
where am I spending my
time, and does it matter?

00:02:47.092 --> 00:02:49.002
And the more that I'm
spending time on things

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.237
that don't matter, that
don't matter to me,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.500
that don't matter to other people,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.453
it's not having an impact somewhere,

00:02:54.453 --> 00:02:57.664
then I drop those things and
move on to something else.

00:02:57.664 --> 00:03:00.148
And you owe it to yourself

00:03:00.148 --> 00:03:03.036
to take the greatness that's within you

00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:05.637
and create something amazing with it

00:03:05.637 --> 00:03:09.215
and stop spending time on
things that do not matter.

00:03:09.215 --> 00:03:11.125
If you spent more time on creating

00:03:11.125 --> 00:03:14.948
amazing and memorable
experiences, you're going to feel

00:03:14.948 --> 00:03:17.839
more fulfilled, you're going
to feel more successful,

00:03:17.839 --> 00:03:19.428
you're going to have a lot more money,

00:03:19.428 --> 00:03:21.016
and you're going to make
a much greater impact

00:03:21.016 --> 00:03:23.788
on the world and the people around you.

00:03:23.788 --> 00:03:25.048
So the question of the day today is,

00:03:25.048 --> 00:03:27.817
I'm curious, what do you love most

00:03:27.817 --> 00:03:30.256
about your business and
what you do every day

00:03:30.256 --> 00:03:32.047
that creates memories?

00:03:32.047 --> 00:03:33.390
Leave it in the comments below.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.015
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:03:35.015 --> 00:03:37.334
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout-out to Tom Torrez.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:38.593
Tom, thank you so much for picking up

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.462
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:40.462 --> 00:03:43.302
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:03:43.302 --> 00:03:44.681
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:44.681 --> 00:03:46.022
I believe in you.

00:03:46.022 --> 00:03:48.143
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:03:48.143 --> 00:03:50.176
and whatever your one word is.

00:03:50.176 --> 00:03:52.375
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:03:52.375 --> 00:03:53.757
for another shot

00:03:53.757 --> 00:03:54.854
of Entspresso.

00:03:54.854 --> 00:03:57.165
♫ I wake up every mornin',

00:03:57.165 --> 00:04:01.063
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'.

00:04:01.063 --> 00:04:02.731
Hey, Believe Nation, as a special bonus,

00:04:02.731 --> 00:04:04.518
for those of you
interested in learning more

00:04:04.518 --> 00:04:06.591
about creating memorable experiences,

00:04:06.591 --> 00:04:09.762
we've lined up a few more
clips that I think will help.

00:04:09.762 --> 00:04:11.471
- Well, I said that the
most important thing

00:04:11.471 --> 00:04:12.755
is the product, and that really is true,

00:04:12.755 --> 00:04:14.139
because you can have all the advertising

00:04:14.139 --> 00:04:15.643
in the world, you can have all the hype,

00:04:15.643 --> 00:04:17.108
and when people go to the store,

00:04:17.108 --> 00:04:19.181
if they try on your pants,
and they don't look good,

00:04:19.181 --> 00:04:21.051
and they don't fit, or
they don't like the fabric,

00:04:21.051 --> 00:04:22.268
they're not going to buy them.

00:04:22.268 --> 00:04:25.449
But, to get them into the
store, to get them there,

00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:27.279
you need the other part of the equation.

00:04:27.279 --> 00:04:30.097
You need to excite them,
and you need, you know,

00:04:30.097 --> 00:04:31.303
pants are pants.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.539
I mean, fashion, you know,
one pair of black pants

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:36.058
and the other pair of
black pants, you know,

00:04:36.058 --> 00:04:38.619
so you have to make fashion aspirational.

00:04:38.619 --> 00:04:40.167
You have to make people believe

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.361
that if they just have those pants,

00:04:42.361 --> 00:04:43.781
their whole life is
going to come together,

00:04:43.781 --> 00:04:45.484
they're going to get that guy
they want, they're going to get

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:46.434
that new job, they're going to get,

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.524
you know, it's because, and that's

00:04:48.524 --> 00:04:50.677
just as much a part of the experience,

00:04:50.677 --> 00:04:53.528
and it actually, again that
sounds like a terrible,

00:04:53.528 --> 00:04:55.558
very calculated thing, but it's not,

00:04:55.558 --> 00:04:59.825
because by creating that
image, you have endowed

00:04:59.825 --> 00:05:03.992
another quality onto that pair
of pants or pair of shoes,

00:05:05.323 --> 00:05:07.441
that really, you know,
makes it something else,

00:05:07.441 --> 00:05:09.353
and makes your experience
of wearing that thing

00:05:09.353 --> 00:05:12.042
something else, and it enhances your life.

00:05:12.042 --> 00:05:13.017
- If it all gives you confidence

00:05:13.017 --> 00:05:15.250
to bring out the best in you,

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.565
if it gives you the confidence
to bring out the best in you,

00:05:17.565 --> 00:05:20.982
then it's contributed to your well-being.

00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:23.907
- Every hotel I've ever built

00:05:23.907 --> 00:05:27.967
has been the highest-grossing
casino in any city

00:05:27.967 --> 00:05:30.122
we've ever been, period.

00:05:30.122 --> 00:05:31.990
The largest amount of money ever won

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.834
by a licensed casino
in the state of Nevada,

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.942
when I built it, was Mirage.

00:05:36.942 --> 00:05:40.638
That record was broken
when we built Bellagio.

00:05:40.638 --> 00:05:42.508
And then, the current record is held

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.582
by Wynn Las Vegas.

00:05:44.582 --> 00:05:48.204
770 million dollars in
casino revenue last year.

00:05:48.204 --> 00:05:51.866
That was more than anybody else
in the history of the state.

00:05:51.866 --> 00:05:56.658
170-odd million with slot
machines, 600 million was tables.

00:05:56.658 --> 00:06:01.297
Of the 600 million in tables,
52% of it was from Asia.

00:06:01.297 --> 00:06:05.464
24% was from Latin America,
24% was from the United States.

00:06:08.027 --> 00:06:09.444
Interesting, huh?

00:06:10.583 --> 00:06:12.861
450 million out of 600 million was

00:06:12.861 --> 00:06:14.978
from outside the United States.

00:06:14.978 --> 00:06:18.145
Why are people from San Paolo, Brazil,

00:06:19.574 --> 00:06:23.881
Rio de Janiero, Buenos
Aires, Bogota Columbia,

00:06:23.881 --> 00:06:26.358
Monterry Mexico, Mexico City,

00:06:26.358 --> 00:06:27.862
these are where we have offices,

00:06:27.862 --> 00:06:29.362
Hong Kong, Taiwan,

00:06:31.735 --> 00:06:32.818
Seoul, Korea,

00:06:33.672 --> 00:06:36.272
Tokyo, and all over mainland China,

00:06:36.272 --> 00:06:40.255
why do they get on airplanes,
fly over other casinos,

00:06:40.255 --> 00:06:42.005
to come to Las Vegas?

00:06:42.895 --> 00:06:46.431
Because of the atmosphere,
because of wonderful service,

00:06:46.431 --> 00:06:49.728
because of a great hotel staff.

00:06:49.728 --> 00:06:52.572
Because it's fun to be
there, whether you gamble

00:06:52.572 --> 00:06:53.655
or you don't.

00:06:54.648 --> 00:06:57.740
And although we broke
the record at 770 million

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.588
for a casino revenue for any licensee

00:07:00.588 --> 00:07:02.781
in the history of Nevada,

00:07:02.781 --> 00:07:06.234
the not-casino revenue
revenue was 860 million.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.484
Over half, yup.

00:07:08.998 --> 00:07:11.684
And it's the 860 that made it possible

00:07:11.684 --> 00:07:12.684
for the 770.

00:07:13.795 --> 00:07:16.311
I'm goin' through all this with you all

00:07:16.311 --> 00:07:18.712
to explain to ya our attitude,

00:07:18.712 --> 00:07:20.904
why we do what we do,

00:07:20.904 --> 00:07:23.996
and what really matters in our business.

00:07:23.996 --> 00:07:27.458
And it's two words, and
everything else is baloney.

00:07:27.458 --> 00:07:29.530
Forget all about the
movies, and the Hollywood,

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.530
and the "eye in the
sky", and the security.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.419
One thing, one thing matters to the state

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:37.419
of Massachusetts, if it cares

00:07:37.419 --> 00:07:40.836
about revenue and jobs, guest experience.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:46.766
If people have a good time,
if they're well-served,

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:50.710
if they're in an atmosphere
that's exciting and stimulating,

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.311
they come back again,
they're willing to pay

00:07:53.311 --> 00:07:55.192
more money next year, a little more

00:07:55.192 --> 00:07:56.691
than they paid this year,

00:07:56.691 --> 00:08:00.813
so that we can cover the
increasing cost of doing business,

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:04.582
unions need increases, people
want to get paid more money,

00:08:04.582 --> 00:08:06.887
cost of living goes up,

00:08:06.887 --> 00:08:10.870
ya get a franchise because
people have a good experience.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.860
And when you give people
a good experience,

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.643
they come from outside the
region into the region.

00:08:16.643 --> 00:08:18.632
And if you want to get
people from over there

00:08:18.632 --> 00:08:21.476
to come over here, you
better build somethin' here

00:08:21.476 --> 00:08:23.304
that's better than there.

00:08:23.304 --> 00:08:25.335
- We collect this year
about eight billion dollars

00:08:25.335 --> 00:08:26.799
of customers' money.

00:08:26.799 --> 00:08:29.238
So thank you, all of you,
for giving us your money.

00:08:29.238 --> 00:08:32.001
And what we do is we say,
that money's in trust

00:08:32.001 --> 00:08:33.180
to create joy.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:36.190
We have to turn that into
the most joy possible.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:38.258
And so we look and we say, for every show,

00:08:38.258 --> 00:08:41.060
if a show costs 100 million
dollars, how much joy,

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.457
how much viewing did it
create amongst all of you?

00:08:43.457 --> 00:08:46.386
If it cost 50 million or
200 million, of course,

00:08:46.386 --> 00:08:48.459
you want different amounts of joy, and so

00:08:48.459 --> 00:08:50.655
we look at it as how
much joy can we create

00:08:50.655 --> 00:08:54.724
of your money, and if we
turn it into joy effectively,

00:08:54.724 --> 00:08:56.105
then you're happy and
you tell your friends

00:08:56.105 --> 00:08:58.219
and we grow and then we
have more money next year

00:08:58.219 --> 00:09:00.214
to turn into more joy.

00:09:00.214 --> 00:09:02.449
So we think ourself like alchemists.

00:09:02.449 --> 00:09:05.861
We take in money, and out comes joy.

00:09:05.861 --> 00:09:07.809
- Add some value.

00:09:07.809 --> 00:09:11.976
There's a true societal and
business value proposition.

00:09:12.928 --> 00:09:14.914
There's a contribution.

00:09:14.914 --> 00:09:18.242
I find, and I don't do this for reasons

00:09:18.242 --> 00:09:21.528
other than the fact that
you can't, long term,

00:09:21.528 --> 00:09:25.913
build a viable business without
making a real contribution.

00:09:25.913 --> 00:09:27.580
Most people look at,

00:09:29.573 --> 00:09:32.870
they can start a business,
do an IPO, make some money,

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:36.120
almost always, that leads to businesses

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:39.007
that are round trips.

00:09:39.007 --> 00:09:41.688
What I call 'em, because
they go up and go down.

00:09:41.688 --> 00:09:44.046
To build a durable business,
you really have to focus

00:09:44.046 --> 00:09:46.067
on the value proposition.

